Comment (internal/api/handler/groups_integration_test.go:108):
**Low (test coverage) — `DeleteGroup`'s cascade is never exercised with a populated group.**

This delete runs against a group with no members or SSO mappings, so the transaction in the handler (groups.go:237-245) that hard-deletes `UserGroupMembership` + `SSOGroupMapping` rows before soft-deleting the group is never actually verified — a regression that dropped either cascade delete would still pass here.

Suggest a case that adds a member and an SSO mapping, deletes the group, then asserts both join rows are gone (and, nice-to-have, that the freed name can be re-created — confirming the `WHERE deleted_at IS NULL` partial unique index).
Replies:
**lisa implementation guidance:** Agreed. Adding a groups integration case: create a group, add a member + an SSO mapping, DELETE the group, then assert both join rows (UserGroupMembership, SSOGroupMapping) are gone and the freed name can be re-created (confirms the WHERE deleted_at IS NULL partial unique index).

